1
00:00:15,641 --> 00:00:17,141
- You know this guy?
- Orlando Diaz.

2
00:00:17,142 --> 00:00:18,893
We were treating him
for DKA when he eloped.

3
00:00:18,894 --> 00:00:20,478
- How far did he fall?
- 20 feet or so.

4
00:00:20,479 --> 00:00:22,313
- Anyone see him pass out?
- No.

5
00:00:22,314 --> 00:00:24,440
They went looking for him after
he didn't answer his radio.

6
00:00:24,441 --> 00:00:25,650
Pupils equal but sluggish.

7
00:00:25,651 --> 00:00:27,026
He left against
medical advice.

8
00:00:27,027 --> 00:00:29,655
On my count, three, two, one.

9
00:00:30,906 --> 00:00:33,199
Dr. Ellis on the case.
Day shift, we got this.

10
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:35,576
- I'm staying.
- Continuity of care.

11
00:00:35,577 --> 00:00:36,953
Dr. Al-Hashimi,
why don't you go cover

12
00:00:36,954 --> 00:00:38,246
sign-out rounds with Dr. Abbot?

13
00:00:38,247 --> 00:00:39,580
- Shen, you too.
- Got it.

14
00:00:39,581 --> 00:00:41,666
OK, let me know
if you need anything.

15
00:00:41,667 --> 00:00:44,252
- Lungs are up bilaterally.
- Pelvis is stable.

16
00:00:44,253 --> 00:00:48,130
Right tib-fib hematoma,
deformed right forearm.

17
00:00:48,131 --> 00:00:50,132
Ruptured TM on the left
with sero-sanguinous fluid.

18
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:51,926
That means
basilar skull fracture.

19
00:00:51,927 --> 00:00:53,719
We've got a diabetic patient,
20-foot fall.

20
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:56,055
BP 204 over 98, pulse 56.

21
00:00:56,056 --> 00:00:57,723
Dr. Mohan, what do those
numbers indicate?

22
00:00:57,724 --> 00:00:59,517
I'm trying
to treat the patient.

23
00:00:59,518 --> 00:01:00,810
It's the Cushing's reflex.

24
00:01:00,811 --> 00:01:02,937
From increased
intracranial pressure.

25
00:01:02,938 --> 00:01:05,273
Yeah, we need to get him
to CT right away.

26
00:01:05,274 --> 00:01:06,941
No free fluid in the belly.

27
00:01:06,942 --> 00:01:10,278
- Any family to notify?
- Wife and three kids.

28
00:01:10,279 --> 00:01:12,363
Is there a card
to sign for Robby?

29
00:01:12,364 --> 00:01:14,407
No, he said
no card, no presents.

30
00:01:14,408 --> 00:01:15,825
Oh. Was there a cake?

31
00:01:15,826 --> 00:01:17,410
Oh, he didn't want
that either.

32
00:01:17,411 --> 00:01:19,370
That sucks.
I need some cake.

33
00:01:19,371 --> 00:01:21,581
Patient was injured
when they raided a restaurant.

34
00:01:21,582 --> 00:01:23,374
And they actually
arrested the nurse?

35
00:01:23,375 --> 00:01:25,918
- With a takedown and zip ties.
- Damn.

36
00:01:25,919 --> 00:01:28,045
Crus, you, uh, know
the computer downtime drill?

37
00:01:28,046 --> 00:01:29,505
Yeah, no biggie.

38
00:01:29,506 --> 00:01:31,173
I prefer to treat 'em
without labs and X-rays.

39
00:01:31,174 --> 00:01:32,675
Welcome back.

40
00:01:32,676 --> 00:01:34,552
If you do have orders
for labs and X-rays,

41
00:01:34,553 --> 00:01:36,637
clipboards go here.

42
00:01:36,638 --> 00:01:39,390
If it's just
nursing orders, here.

43
00:01:39,391 --> 00:01:41,183
Please write neatly,
for God's sake.

44
00:01:41,184 --> 00:01:43,728
Oh, Monica, this is Nazely,
new intern.

45
00:01:43,729 --> 00:01:46,523
- I don't need to know that.
- So nice to meet you.

46
00:01:47,691 --> 00:01:49,400
Looks like you and me, Jack.

47
00:01:49,401 --> 00:01:50,860
Yeah, who's our senior?

48
00:01:50,861 --> 00:01:53,988
- Dr. Henderson.
- Excellent.

49
00:01:53,989 --> 00:01:55,865
Night shift's on Crus control.

50
00:01:55,866 --> 00:01:57,992
You hear
ICE brought us a patient?

51
00:01:57,993 --> 00:01:59,785
Oh, yeah?
How'd that go?

52
00:01:59,786 --> 00:02:00,911
There was some
collateral damage.

53
00:02:00,912 --> 00:02:02,413
They arrested Jesse.

54
00:02:02,414 --> 00:02:04,415
- For what?
- Assaulting a federal officer.

55
00:02:04,416 --> 00:02:05,958
Are you fucking kidding me?

56
00:02:05,959 --> 00:02:07,335
Oh, Dr. Al-Hashimi,

57
00:02:07,336 --> 00:02:09,546
this is Nazely Toomarian--
new intern.

58
00:02:16,345 --> 00:02:18,262
OK, everybody,
let's huddle up.

59
00:02:18,263 --> 00:02:19,597
Before we start,

60
00:02:19,598 --> 00:02:21,223
let me address
the elephant in the room.

61
00:02:21,224 --> 00:02:23,017
For those of you
who don't know,

62
00:02:23,018 --> 00:02:24,477
Jesse tried to intervene

63
00:02:24,478 --> 00:02:26,270
when a federal agent
was handling his patient,

64
00:02:26,271 --> 00:02:28,648
and both he and the patient
were taken away by ICE.

65
00:02:28,649 --> 00:02:30,316
- Did he punch the guy?
- No.

66
00:02:30,317 --> 00:02:32,735
He put out a hand to stop him,
made physical contact.

67
00:02:32,736 --> 00:02:34,320
It was a little bit more than that.

68
00:02:34,321 --> 00:02:35,905
The hospital lawyers
are on the case,

69
00:02:35,906 --> 00:02:38,240
and we will brief the staff
every 12 hours

70
00:02:38,241 --> 00:02:39,992
at sign-out rounds
with an official update.

71
00:02:39,993 --> 00:02:42,495
In the meantime,
don't feed the rumor mill.

72
00:02:42,496 --> 00:02:44,830
You may have also heard
that new grad nurse Emma here

73
00:02:44,831 --> 00:02:47,333
- was assaulted by a patient.
- I--I'm fine.

74
00:02:47,334 --> 00:02:48,959
Please don't forget
"code hula hoop,"

75
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:50,294
and with risky patients,

76
00:02:50,295 --> 00:02:52,630
always keep a path
to the door clear.

77
00:02:52,631 --> 00:02:54,298
Sounds like
one hell of a day.

78
00:02:54,299 --> 00:02:56,133
And we're still dealing
with downtime,

79
00:02:56,134 --> 00:02:58,302
so day shift should brief
night residents

80
00:02:58,303 --> 00:02:59,637
about the protocol--

81
00:02:59,638 --> 00:03:00,596
Hey!

82
00:03:00,597 --> 00:03:02,264
Oh, all right!

83
00:03:02,265 --> 00:03:04,475
Oh, thank God.

84
00:03:04,476 --> 00:03:05,851
Yeah, not so fast.

85
00:03:05,852 --> 00:03:07,728
Every chart
from the last five hours

86
00:03:07,729 --> 00:03:10,064
needs to be scanned into
the Electronic Health Record

87
00:03:10,065 --> 00:03:12,108
and checked for accuracy...

88
00:03:12,109 --> 00:03:14,276
- Um, whose job is that?
- Day shift.

89
00:03:14,277 --> 00:03:16,237
With a completed
and signed T-sheet.

90
00:03:16,238 --> 00:03:17,947
- Are you kidding me?
- That's gonna take forever.

91
00:03:17,948 --> 00:03:19,699
We will set up stations
for scanning.

92
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:21,492
OK, everybody,
let's get moving.

93
00:03:21,493 --> 00:03:23,661
Triage is 20 behind.
Gotta help 'em clean up.

94
00:03:23,662 --> 00:03:24,912
I'm skipping rounds.

95
00:03:24,913 --> 00:03:26,747
Consider yourself lucky.

96
00:03:26,748 --> 00:03:27,916
Should we join them?

97
00:03:29,334 --> 00:03:31,043
Might as well
witness the magic.

98
00:03:31,044 --> 00:03:33,295
It's like changing of the guard
at Buckingham Palace.

99
00:03:33,296 --> 00:03:35,172
Except we're allowed
to smile.

100
00:03:35,173 --> 00:03:37,384
"Smile though
your heart is aching."

101
00:03:38,552 --> 00:03:39,635
Plain films, right tib-fib

102
00:03:39,636 --> 00:03:41,595
and right forearm after CT.

103
00:03:41,596 --> 00:03:43,597
Got the chem-8.
Blood sugar's 284.

104
00:03:43,598 --> 00:03:46,225
That's not too bad.
Potassium looks good.

105
00:03:46,226 --> 00:03:48,477
Mm-hmm.
Anion gap's up at 14.

106
00:03:48,478 --> 00:03:49,729
It was 24 this morning.

107
00:03:49,730 --> 00:03:51,397
He's definitely improving.

108
00:03:51,398 --> 00:03:52,773
The DKA is resolving.

109
00:03:52,774 --> 00:03:54,400
So what made him pass out?

110
00:03:54,401 --> 00:03:56,235
It's hot as hell out there.

111
00:03:56,236 --> 00:03:58,404
He could have been dehydrated
from sweating.

112
00:03:58,405 --> 00:04:01,866
Or he could have had
an N-STEMI or a posterior CVA.

113
00:04:01,867 --> 00:04:03,326
Ready to roll.

114
00:04:05,078 --> 00:04:07,788
- I can babysit him at CT.
- Thank you.

115
00:04:07,789 --> 00:04:10,000
I'll stay
in case he needs the OR.

116
00:04:11,835 --> 00:04:13,794
Hey, we're back up.

117
00:04:13,795 --> 00:04:15,796
It's about time.

118
00:04:15,797 --> 00:04:17,256
- Ooh, Robby.
- Yeah.

119
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:19,467
I got intel on where
ICE has taken Jesse.

120
00:04:19,468 --> 00:04:20,718
Intel from who?

121
00:04:20,719 --> 00:04:22,595
Uh, my brother-in-law's
a cop.

122
00:04:22,596 --> 00:04:24,930
So he'll be processed
at DHS Southside

123
00:04:24,931 --> 00:04:27,433
and then transferred
to ICE detention in Clearfield.

124
00:04:27,434 --> 00:04:28,726
Clearfield?
That's two hours away.

125
00:04:28,727 --> 00:04:30,227
Mm-hmm.

126
00:04:30,228 --> 00:04:32,354
OK, I'll let
the hospital attorneys know.

127
00:04:32,355 --> 00:04:34,273
- How are you doing, Oliver?
- Alive and kicking.

128
00:04:34,274 --> 00:04:35,649
Uh, Mr. Haas.

129
00:04:35,650 --> 00:04:37,943
Pulmonary edema
after missed dialysis,

130
00:04:37,944 --> 00:04:40,529
now stable with his son Mason
at the bedside.

131
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:42,156
- Hello.
- I'm Dr. Shen.

132
00:04:42,157 --> 00:04:43,365
I'll be back.

133
00:04:43,366 --> 00:04:44,408
Dialysis tech says

134
00:04:44,409 --> 00:04:46,202
I'm off the machine at 10:42.

135
00:04:46,203 --> 00:04:48,329
Hit the call light,
and I'll come running.

136
00:04:48,330 --> 00:04:50,415
South 21 next...

137
00:04:52,375 --> 00:04:54,210
Mr. Digby.

138
00:04:54,211 --> 00:04:55,795
J-just Digby.

139
00:04:55,796 --> 00:04:57,463
Dr. Mohan's patient.

140
00:04:57,464 --> 00:04:59,673
Forearm cellulitis,
admit med-surge.

141
00:04:59,674 --> 00:05:01,258
- Awaiting a bed.
- I can take him.

142
00:05:01,259 --> 00:05:03,093
Sold to Dr. Toomarian.

143
00:05:03,094 --> 00:05:05,513
Moving right along.

144
00:05:05,514 --> 00:05:07,306
Get enough to eat?

145
00:05:07,307 --> 00:05:09,642
We'll be back.

146
00:05:09,643 --> 00:05:13,062
Lillian Stegman.
Tweaked her knee water-skiing.

147
00:05:13,063 --> 00:05:15,105
Doing a 360
off a 5-foot ramp.

148
00:05:15,106 --> 00:05:16,565
Ooh, respect.

149
00:05:16,566 --> 00:05:17,900
X-rays ordered in triage.

150
00:05:17,901 --> 00:05:19,193
That was hours ago.

151
00:05:19,194 --> 00:05:21,403
Ma'am,
I'm Dr. Crus Henderson.

152
00:05:21,404 --> 00:05:23,656
Let's get you home real fast.

153
00:05:23,657 --> 00:05:25,407
- That would be wonderful.
- OK, heading to North.

154
00:05:25,408 --> 00:05:27,117
Thank you.

155
00:05:27,118 --> 00:05:29,662
Looks like our first scanning
station is almost ready.

156
00:05:29,663 --> 00:05:32,414
Whitaker, Santos, after rounds,
this will be your post.

157
00:05:32,415 --> 00:05:35,084
- Seriously?
- For... how long?

158
00:05:35,085 --> 00:05:37,211
Till we mop up this mess.

159
00:05:37,212 --> 00:05:38,879
And away we go.

160
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:41,048
All right,
now you know everything

161
00:05:41,049 --> 00:05:42,258
there is to know about rounds.

162
00:05:42,259 --> 00:05:43,425
Fascinating, right?

163
00:05:43,426 --> 00:05:45,594
Uh... yeah.

164
00:05:45,595 --> 00:05:47,806
Here, I got something
better for you.

165
00:05:49,599 --> 00:05:52,476
So, Digby, we're gonna find you
some new clothes,

166
00:05:52,477 --> 00:05:54,270
but my friend Emma and I
wondered if you'd like

167
00:05:54,271 --> 00:05:56,897
to get cleaned up a bit first.

168
00:05:56,898 --> 00:05:58,649
I already had a shower.

169
00:05:58,650 --> 00:06:00,276
I know, and you look good.

170
00:06:00,277 --> 00:06:02,361
But the offer also comes
with a shave and a haircut,

171
00:06:02,362 --> 00:06:03,612
if you're interested.

172
00:06:03,613 --> 00:06:04,822
No pressure--like I said,

173
00:06:04,823 --> 00:06:05,991
you already look great.

174
00:06:07,409 --> 00:06:10,411
- Sure, I guess.
- Fantastic.

175
00:06:10,412 --> 00:06:12,413
All right, kid, fill that basin
with some warm water

176
00:06:12,414 --> 00:06:14,040
and lather him up.

177
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:19,461
- Hey, stay safe out there.
- Back at you in here.

178
00:06:19,462 --> 00:06:21,463
Hey, Cary.

179
00:06:21,464 --> 00:06:23,591
You were on scene
with Orlando, right?

180
00:06:23,592 --> 00:06:26,010
Did you notice anything
about his fall?

181
00:06:26,011 --> 00:06:27,511
Like what?

182
00:06:27,512 --> 00:06:30,681
Like, um, if there was
a break in the railing

183
00:06:30,682 --> 00:06:33,684
or if there were
security cameras?

184
00:06:33,685 --> 00:06:35,269
Too busy working on the guy--

185
00:06:35,270 --> 00:06:37,730
IV, intubation,
backboard, splint.

186
00:06:37,731 --> 00:06:38,898
Thanks.

187
00:06:38,899 --> 00:06:40,524
Oh, two names is a start.

188
00:06:40,525 --> 00:06:42,276
Pretty soon, we'll retire
the clipboards.

189
00:06:42,277 --> 00:06:43,611
Baby Jane Doe in Pedes?

190
00:06:43,612 --> 00:06:45,487
Uh, yeah, abandoned

191
00:06:45,488 --> 00:06:48,240
in the waiting room bathroom
at 7:30 a.m.

192
00:06:48,241 --> 00:06:50,701
- Safe haven drop-off?
- No, she's too old for that.

193
00:06:50,702 --> 00:06:52,536
- At least two months.
- I'll take her.

194
00:06:52,537 --> 00:06:54,705
Awaiting foster placement
by CYF.

195
00:06:54,706 --> 00:06:57,041
- What if the mom comes back?
- Call the cops.

196
00:06:57,042 --> 00:06:58,500
Day shift,
get to work scanning.

197
00:06:58,501 --> 00:07:00,044
Night shift, the room numbers

198
00:07:00,045 --> 00:07:02,212
on top of the dry-erase board
need a doctor.

199
00:07:02,213 --> 00:07:05,132
- Who's in BH-1?
- Psych hold, danger to self.

200
00:07:05,133 --> 00:07:06,592
What's the story?

201
00:07:06,593 --> 00:07:08,469
Doctors King and Langdon
were on the case.

202
00:07:08,470 --> 00:07:10,721
It's a sad story--
she says her 5-year-old

203
00:07:10,722 --> 00:07:12,598
snuck into the back seat
of the car to take a nap.

204
00:07:12,599 --> 00:07:14,266
Heat stroke.

205
00:07:14,267 --> 00:07:16,644
Mom was extremely distraught.
Walked out into traffic.

206
00:07:16,645 --> 00:07:18,187
Grady Barnhill, wheezing

207
00:07:18,188 --> 00:07:19,813
and not responding
to albuterol.

208
00:07:19,814 --> 00:07:21,690
Pulse ox 87. His mother, Naomi.

209
00:07:21,691 --> 00:07:23,901
- OK, Trauma Two's open.
- On our way.

210
00:07:23,902 --> 00:07:26,403
- Uh, Mom, history of asthma?
- His whole life.

211
00:07:26,404 --> 00:07:28,530
- Never this bad.
- Barely moving air.

212
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:31,158
Using all his
accessory muscles.

213
00:07:31,159 --> 00:07:32,618
Call RT!

214
00:07:32,619 --> 00:07:35,371
Uh, continuous nebs,
20 milligrams an hour.

215
00:07:35,372 --> 00:07:36,872
We have a home nebulizer.

216
00:07:36,873 --> 00:07:39,750
I've been giving him
albuterol every hour.

217
00:07:39,751 --> 00:07:40,876
Ready?

218
00:07:40,877 --> 00:07:43,796
On my count, one, two, three.

219
00:07:43,797 --> 00:07:45,255
Does he take
any other medications?

220
00:07:45,256 --> 00:07:46,757
Just the albuterol.

221
00:07:46,758 --> 00:07:48,300
He used to be on montelukast
and Symbicort.

222
00:07:48,301 --> 00:07:49,885
Why did you stop that?

223
00:07:49,886 --> 00:07:51,929
Because he lost his Medicaid
two months ago.

224
00:07:51,930 --> 00:07:53,764
He's so tight,
nothing's getting through.

225
00:07:53,765 --> 00:07:55,349
- Mel, EpiPen.
- On it.

226
00:07:55,350 --> 00:07:56,850
0.3 milligrams.

227
00:07:56,851 --> 00:07:59,979
That may open his lungs
so the nebs can work.

228
00:07:59,980 --> 00:08:01,982
All right, Grady,
shot in the thigh.

229
00:08:07,028 --> 00:08:08,862
Hey.

230
00:08:08,863 --> 00:08:10,322
Something to scan?

231
00:08:10,323 --> 00:08:11,865
Critical labs on North Three.

232
00:08:11,866 --> 00:08:13,450
Oh, it's, uh--
it's not my patient.

233
00:08:13,451 --> 00:08:14,703
She's about to be.

234
00:08:16,621 --> 00:08:18,956
I'm, uh--
I'm off the clock, so...

235
00:08:18,957 --> 00:08:21,625
These were ordered
three hours ago from triage,

236
00:08:21,626 --> 00:08:24,086
so, technically,
she is a day-shift patient.

237
00:08:24,087 --> 00:08:25,379
Just get the intern started.

238
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:26,922
I got a meeting upstairs
with admin

239
00:08:26,923 --> 00:08:28,924
to get things back on track.

240
00:08:28,925 --> 00:08:30,676
Sorry.
Everyone else is tied up.

241
00:08:30,677 --> 00:08:32,052
That's OK.

242
00:08:32,053 --> 00:08:33,262
How'd you get stuck
on night shift

243
00:08:33,263 --> 00:08:34,430
for your first rotation?

244
00:08:34,431 --> 00:08:35,889
Just lucky, I guess.

245
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:37,350
Yeah, if you like
a good horror movie.

246
00:08:38,768 --> 00:08:40,728
- Where was med school?
- Uh, UC Irvine.

247
00:08:40,729 --> 00:08:42,521
- California, right?
- Yep.

248
00:08:42,522 --> 00:08:43,772
Pittsburgh's
a little different.

249
00:08:43,773 --> 00:08:44,982
Yeah, a lot more humidity.

250
00:08:44,983 --> 00:08:46,066
Yeah, that'll go away

251
00:08:46,067 --> 00:08:47,985
with your first foot of snow.

252
00:08:47,986 --> 00:08:50,779
Uh, hi, Mrs. Davis.

253
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:52,823
I am Dr. McKay.
This is Doctor...

254
00:08:52,824 --> 00:08:55,075
- Toomarian.
- Hello.

255
00:08:55,076 --> 00:08:58,203
Uh, your labs show a lot
of inflammation in your liver.

256
00:08:58,204 --> 00:09:01,582
- Is that why I'm so nauseated?
- Definitely, yeah.

257
00:09:01,583 --> 00:09:04,668
Have you, um, noticed a change
in your skin coloration?

258
00:09:04,669 --> 00:09:06,712
I've been using
this bronzing cream

259
00:09:06,713 --> 00:09:09,381
so I don't look like a ghost
in my bathing suit.

260
00:09:09,382 --> 00:09:11,341
Do you remember
the name of the bronzer?

261
00:09:11,342 --> 00:09:12,885
It could have a chemical
that can cause--

262
00:09:12,886 --> 00:09:14,928
Oh, no, no,
it's 100% natural.

263
00:09:14,929 --> 00:09:18,182
- It's DHA from sugar beets.
- OK.

264
00:09:18,183 --> 00:09:20,350
Why would my liver
be inflamed?

265
00:09:20,351 --> 00:09:22,311
Uh, there's a lot
of possibilities.

266
00:09:22,312 --> 00:09:24,146
Are you taking any
prescription medications?

267
00:09:24,147 --> 00:09:25,147
Not a single one.

268
00:09:25,148 --> 00:09:26,732
- Tylenol?
- God, no.

269
00:09:26,733 --> 00:09:28,942
We have to ask everybody
about injection drug use.

270
00:09:28,943 --> 00:09:30,069
Never.

271
00:09:30,070 --> 00:09:31,737
Raw clams or oysters?

272
00:09:31,738 --> 00:09:33,572
I'm a vegan.

273
00:09:33,573 --> 00:09:35,783
One step at a time, OK?

274
00:09:35,784 --> 00:09:36,868
We'll be back.

275
00:09:38,286 --> 00:09:40,204
Digby, Haas,
now on the big board.

276
00:09:40,205 --> 00:09:41,205
Progress.

277
00:09:41,206 --> 00:09:42,206
So he's just been waiting

278
00:09:42,207 --> 00:09:43,874
in the hall the whole time?

279
00:09:43,875 --> 00:09:46,753
OK, well, can you maybe
get to him next?

280
00:09:48,046 --> 00:09:49,089
Thank you.

281
00:09:50,215 --> 00:09:51,882
Duke goes to CT,
and they bump him.

282
00:09:51,883 --> 00:09:54,384
Yeah, he may end up
waiting for hours over there.

283
00:09:54,385 --> 00:09:56,887
Oh, look at that.
7:15 already.

284
00:09:56,888 --> 00:09:58,847
Just a few more loose ends
to tie up.

285
00:09:58,848 --> 00:10:02,059
You got more loose ends
than a macramé wall hanging.

286
00:10:02,060 --> 00:10:04,353
My mom had one.
Took up the whole goddamn wall.

287
00:10:04,354 --> 00:10:06,063
Seriously, you should
think about signing out

288
00:10:06,064 --> 00:10:07,856
- and hitting the road.
- Yeah, maybe you should too.

289
00:10:07,857 --> 00:10:09,608
Oh, that's right,
you sent Lena home.

290
00:10:09,609 --> 00:10:11,485
Are you planning on
calling in a replacement,

291
00:10:11,486 --> 00:10:13,278
or are you just gonna work
till sunrise?

292
00:10:13,279 --> 00:10:14,696
If I have to.

293
00:10:14,697 --> 00:10:16,782
Oh, so you get to go
the extra mile,

294
00:10:16,783 --> 00:10:19,284
and the rest of us just get
accused of being martyrs.

295
00:10:19,285 --> 00:10:20,578
- Robby.
- Excuse me.

296
00:10:22,622 --> 00:10:24,581
- What's the word?
- No subdural, no epidural.

297
00:10:24,582 --> 00:10:26,583
Diffuse brain swelling
with effacement

298
00:10:26,584 --> 00:10:28,293
and compression
of the ventricles.

299
00:10:28,294 --> 00:10:30,504
C-spine?
Chest-abdomen-pelvis?

300
00:10:30,505 --> 00:10:32,798
Uh, left pulmonary contusion,
no intra-abdominal hemorrhage.

301
00:10:32,799 --> 00:10:33,966
Which means I'm off the hook.

302
00:10:33,967 --> 00:10:35,425
I'll send Neurosurgery down.

303
00:10:35,426 --> 00:10:37,970
If he doesn't need the OR,
why Neurosurgery?

304
00:10:37,971 --> 00:10:39,388
- Wait and see.
- Let's get busy.

305
00:10:39,389 --> 00:10:40,639
CVP and an art line.

306
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:43,726
Orlando.
Orlando, squeeze my hand.

307
00:10:44,894 --> 00:10:46,186
Open your eyes.

308
00:10:46,187 --> 00:10:48,730
We already know his GCS
is going to be three.

309
00:10:48,731 --> 00:10:50,732
Hey, Javadi,
anti-seizure prophylaxis?

310
00:10:50,733 --> 00:10:52,734
- Keppra, 20 migs per kilo.
- Mixing it now.

311
00:10:52,735 --> 00:10:54,403
Gotta get this brain swelling
down, Samira.

312
00:10:54,404 --> 00:10:55,488
How we gonna do that?

313
00:10:56,781 --> 00:10:58,365
- Samira?
- What?

314
00:10:58,366 --> 00:11:01,577
We have to lower
the intracranial pressure.

315
00:11:01,578 --> 00:11:03,287
- Mannitol.
- Not the best.

316
00:11:03,288 --> 00:11:04,621
Can cause diuresis
and hypotension.

317
00:11:04,622 --> 00:11:05,998
Then hypertonic saline.

318
00:11:05,999 --> 00:11:08,418
23%.
50 cc's through a central line.

319
00:11:10,336 --> 00:11:11,920
Still tight as a drum.

320
00:11:11,921 --> 00:11:13,046
Five minutes since the epi.

321
00:11:13,047 --> 00:11:14,423
He can have one more EpiPen.

322
00:11:14,424 --> 00:11:16,175
Sats are borderline, 87.

323
00:11:16,176 --> 00:11:17,593
How about BiPap?
10 over 5.

324
00:11:17,594 --> 00:11:19,761
Yes, with in-line nebs.

325
00:11:19,762 --> 00:11:21,597
All right, Grady,
shot number two.

326
00:11:21,598 --> 00:11:23,807
Might as well throw in
some magnesium, 50 per kilo.

327
00:11:23,808 --> 00:11:25,142
I'm sorry.
He's not ventilating.

328
00:11:25,143 --> 00:11:26,518
We should be ready to intubate.

329
00:11:26,519 --> 00:11:27,895
With an asthma patient?

330
00:11:27,896 --> 00:11:29,813
There's a high risk
of cardiac arrest.

331
00:11:29,814 --> 00:11:32,065
Naomi, has he ever been put
on a breathing machine before?

332
00:11:32,066 --> 00:11:33,734
- Never.
- Hospitalized?

333
00:11:33,735 --> 00:11:35,652
No, we could always break him
with the Symbicort.

334
00:11:35,653 --> 00:11:37,112
We're gonna give
the current treatment

335
00:11:37,113 --> 00:11:39,157
a few more minutes to help him
turn the corner.

336
00:11:42,327 --> 00:11:44,244
I could probably
do this myself

337
00:11:44,245 --> 00:11:45,662
now that my cast is off.

338
00:11:45,663 --> 00:11:47,581
Oh, that's OK.

339
00:11:47,582 --> 00:11:49,209
I don't mind.

340
00:11:53,129 --> 00:11:55,006
How long have you
been a nurse?

341
00:11:56,424 --> 00:11:58,092
This is my first day.

342
00:12:00,803 --> 00:12:02,805
You're doing really good.

343
00:12:04,766 --> 00:12:06,309
Thank you.

344
00:12:10,313 --> 00:12:12,105
- Oh, shit, you OK?
- Yeah.

345
00:12:12,106 --> 00:12:13,607
There's water on the floor.

346
00:12:13,608 --> 00:12:15,108
Sorry!
I--I might have spilled.

347
00:12:15,109 --> 00:12:16,526
Yeah, no worries.

348
00:12:16,527 --> 00:12:18,570
We're gonna have to sort
these all by patient

349
00:12:18,571 --> 00:12:20,364
before we scan them.

350
00:12:20,365 --> 00:12:23,033
Is, uh, Joy still around?

351
00:12:23,034 --> 00:12:25,702
I heard she left at 6:59.

352
00:12:25,703 --> 00:12:27,704
- Smart girl.
- Mm-hmm.

353
00:12:27,705 --> 00:12:29,873
You know what? Find Ogilvie.
He's such an ass-kisser.

354
00:12:29,874 --> 00:12:31,541
He might stay and scan
all the charts himself.

355
00:12:31,542 --> 00:12:33,710
Oh, he, uh, scrubbed in
in the OR,

356
00:12:33,711 --> 00:12:35,629
scrubbed in
on the ruptured triple-A.

357
00:12:35,630 --> 00:12:37,339
Oh, the kidney stone
that wasn't.

358
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:39,133
That'll be four hours at least.

359
00:12:41,094 --> 00:12:44,513
So are you still going
to Amy's after work?

360
00:12:44,514 --> 00:12:46,431
Yeah, maybe just
for tonight,

361
00:12:46,432 --> 00:12:48,726
after Robby briefs me
on all the house stuff.

362
00:12:49,852 --> 00:12:51,271
Sounds fun.

363
00:12:52,689 --> 00:12:54,690
When he asked,
it was hard to say no.

364
00:12:54,691 --> 00:12:56,025
Sure.

365
00:12:58,278 --> 00:13:00,529
It's gonna be very weird
without him here.

366
00:13:00,530 --> 00:13:01,947
Yeah.

367
00:13:01,948 --> 00:13:04,491
You think Dr. Al-Hashimi
can handle it?

368
00:13:04,492 --> 00:13:06,034
In a word, no.

369
00:13:06,035 --> 00:13:07,452
She's smart.

370
00:13:07,453 --> 00:13:08,745
It takes more than that.

371
00:13:08,746 --> 00:13:10,372
Yeah, well, at least

372
00:13:10,373 --> 00:13:11,748
it's only three months.

373
00:13:11,749 --> 00:13:13,875
Yeah, three long months.

374
00:13:13,876 --> 00:13:15,503
Then you need to find
a new home.

375
00:13:16,462 --> 00:13:17,921
Not necessarily.

376
00:13:17,922 --> 00:13:20,007
I mean, if I wanted,
I could just check on

377
00:13:20,008 --> 00:13:23,093
Robby's house once
or twice a day, you know.

378
00:13:23,094 --> 00:13:24,762
Why would you do that?

379
00:13:26,139 --> 00:13:28,266
I don't know. Why not?

380
00:13:31,352 --> 00:13:32,811
Hypertonic's in.

381
00:13:32,812 --> 00:13:34,938
Maintenance LR in the AC.

382
00:13:34,939 --> 00:13:36,732
Looks like a halo sign.

383
00:13:36,733 --> 00:13:39,318
Cerebrospinal fluid
from a basilar skull fracture.

384
00:13:39,319 --> 00:13:43,322
The halo sign is neither
sensitive nor specific for CSF.

385
00:13:43,323 --> 00:13:45,615
Saline, tap water,
and runny noses

386
00:13:45,616 --> 00:13:46,825
all separate from blood.

387
00:13:46,826 --> 00:13:48,327
- Hello, Linda.
- Robby.

388
00:13:48,328 --> 00:13:50,787
Division chief working
on a holiday weekend.

389
00:13:50,788 --> 00:13:52,914
Well, somebody's got to.

390
00:13:52,915 --> 00:13:55,709
Saw the scans.
This guy needs an EVD.

391
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:58,003
External ventricular drain
to take down the pressure.

392
00:13:58,004 --> 00:14:01,256
Because CPP equals
"MAP" minus ICP.

393
00:14:01,257 --> 00:14:03,925
Cerebral perfusion pressure
in the brain

394
00:14:03,926 --> 00:14:05,844
equals mean arterial
blood pressure

395
00:14:05,845 --> 00:14:07,346
minus the pressure
in the skull.

396
00:14:07,347 --> 00:14:09,056
ICP less than 22

397
00:14:09,057 --> 00:14:11,600
predicts survival
and favorable outcome.

398
00:14:11,601 --> 00:14:15,979
CPP from 60 to 70 reduces
morbidity and mortality.

399
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:17,397
Can somebody assist?

400
00:14:17,398 --> 00:14:18,565
Dr. Mohan?

401
00:14:18,566 --> 00:14:19,650
I'm good.

402
00:14:20,777 --> 00:14:22,361
Samira, you should
lend a hand.

403
00:14:22,362 --> 00:14:24,112
I said I'm good.

404
00:14:24,113 --> 00:14:26,990
- Javadi?
- I don't think so.

405
00:14:26,991 --> 00:14:28,533
Javadi?

406
00:14:28,534 --> 00:14:31,953
As in, daughter
of Raymond and Eileen?

407
00:14:31,954 --> 00:14:34,414
I was at your mother's
baby shower.

408
00:14:34,415 --> 00:14:35,374
She was a resident.

409
00:14:35,375 --> 00:14:36,751
You were in utero.

410
00:14:38,252 --> 00:14:39,378
I don't know how
she got through

411
00:14:39,379 --> 00:14:41,171
motherhood and training.

412
00:14:41,172 --> 00:14:42,756
Feel free to join me.

413
00:14:42,757 --> 00:14:44,633
Oh, my--my shift was over
a while ago.

414
00:14:44,634 --> 00:14:46,093
OK.

415
00:14:46,094 --> 00:14:48,136
Masks all around.
Two sterile gowns.

416
00:14:48,137 --> 00:14:50,764
We brought the surgical towels.
Just need some Betadine.

417
00:14:50,765 --> 00:14:52,350
This is kind of
an amazing opportunity.

418
00:14:53,518 --> 00:14:54,810
I'm exhausted.

419
00:14:54,811 --> 00:14:56,770
The Chief of Neurosurgery
is here.

420
00:14:56,771 --> 00:14:58,230
She's kind of a legend.

421
00:14:58,231 --> 00:15:00,273
Maybe one of the night
residents can do it.

422
00:15:00,274 --> 00:15:02,526
Is this about
the volvulus case from earlier?

423
00:15:02,527 --> 00:15:04,111
'Cause if it is,
you made a mistake.

424
00:15:04,112 --> 00:15:06,029
You need to move on.

425
00:15:06,030 --> 00:15:07,697
I do not want to come back here
and find that

426
00:15:07,698 --> 00:15:10,909
you've applied
for a residency in derm.

427
00:15:10,910 --> 00:15:13,578
Step up to the plate. Do it.

428
00:15:13,579 --> 00:15:14,788
Javadi will assist.

429
00:15:14,789 --> 00:15:16,456
Excellent.

430
00:15:16,457 --> 00:15:18,208
You know, I think Eileen did
her first EVD with me

431
00:15:18,209 --> 00:15:20,670
back when I was a brand-new
assistant professor.

432
00:15:22,088 --> 00:15:23,506
Time flies.

433
00:15:26,467 --> 00:15:27,592
How you doing, Grady?

434
00:15:27,593 --> 00:15:29,052
Still retracting.

435
00:15:29,053 --> 00:15:30,762
- Any improvement?
- Not really.

436
00:15:30,763 --> 00:15:31,806
You feeling tired?

437
00:15:33,683 --> 00:15:36,268
- Do we have Aerogen in the ED?
- Just in the unit.

438
00:15:36,269 --> 00:15:37,894
How fast can you get back?

439
00:15:37,895 --> 00:15:39,062
Two minutes
if I take the stairs.

440
00:15:39,063 --> 00:15:40,105
Go.

441
00:15:40,106 --> 00:15:41,440
Uh, Aerogen?

442
00:15:41,441 --> 00:15:43,400
It has a 5-millimeter mesh

443
00:15:43,401 --> 00:15:46,571
that vibrates
over 120,000 times per second.

444
00:15:51,742 --> 00:15:53,077
Dr. Al-Hashimi?

445
00:15:57,415 --> 00:15:58,833
You OK?

446
00:16:01,294 --> 00:16:03,296
Uh, you were telling us
about Aerogen.

447
00:16:04,464 --> 00:16:05,798
Dr. Shen can explain.

448
00:16:07,216 --> 00:16:10,177
It produces droplets
in the 2- to 5-micron range

449
00:16:10,178 --> 00:16:12,096
for medication delivery.

450
00:16:19,395 --> 00:16:21,938
- How's it going?
- Just about to start.

451
00:16:21,939 --> 00:16:23,148
Securing the art line here.

452
00:16:23,149 --> 00:16:25,400
Measure twice, cut once.

453
00:16:25,401 --> 00:16:29,196
We enter 11 centimeters
back from the nasion,

454
00:16:29,197 --> 00:16:30,822
3 centimeters lateral.

455
00:16:30,823 --> 00:16:32,407
Without any direct imaging?

456
00:16:32,408 --> 00:16:35,452
No, straight shot
into the lateral ventricle--

457
00:16:35,453 --> 00:16:39,039
tried and true since 1890.

458
00:16:39,040 --> 00:16:41,334
OK, go ahead with the incision.

459
00:16:42,877 --> 00:16:45,086
Hey, you worked
with Dr. Al-Hashimi at the VA.

460
00:16:45,087 --> 00:16:46,213
I did.

461
00:16:46,214 --> 00:16:47,714
For how long?

462
00:16:47,715 --> 00:16:49,674
During my R2 rotation

463
00:16:49,675 --> 00:16:51,802
and then one again last year.

464
00:16:55,223 --> 00:16:58,391
OK. Hand drill's all set.

465
00:16:58,392 --> 00:16:59,809
Maybe you should do
this part.

466
00:16:59,810 --> 00:17:01,186
No, no, there's
a safety stop here.

467
00:17:01,187 --> 00:17:02,687
You can't go too deep.

468
00:17:02,688 --> 00:17:04,649
It's not brain surgery.

469
00:17:06,901 --> 00:17:08,110
OK.

470
00:17:11,322 --> 00:17:13,156
- Stay perpendicular.
- OK.

471
00:17:13,157 --> 00:17:15,116
Good.

472
00:17:15,117 --> 00:17:16,868
All right, now, four turns

473
00:17:16,869 --> 00:17:18,078
to get through
the outer table...

474
00:17:18,079 --> 00:17:19,371
- Yep.
- Then half turns

475
00:17:19,372 --> 00:17:20,957
till you penetrate the skull.

476
00:17:31,801 --> 00:17:35,470
Three, four.

477
00:17:35,471 --> 00:17:36,722
One...

478
00:17:38,724 --> 00:17:40,392
Holy smoke!

479
00:17:40,393 --> 00:17:43,812
I thought it was Tom Cruise
for a second over here.

480
00:17:43,813 --> 00:17:46,856
Nice job.
How's that feel, Digby?

481
00:17:46,857 --> 00:17:48,441
- Pretty good.
- I bet.

482
00:17:48,442 --> 00:17:49,734
What do you say we trim up

483
00:17:49,735 --> 00:17:51,445
those gorgeous locks
of yours now?

484
00:17:53,155 --> 00:17:55,198
I don't like having
my hair cut.

485
00:17:55,199 --> 00:17:58,535
I get it, Rapunzel,
but you need your ears lowered.

486
00:17:58,536 --> 00:18:00,662
You'll feel better
with a fresh summer look

487
00:18:00,663 --> 00:18:02,665
that won't go unnoticed
by the ladies.

488
00:18:04,584 --> 00:18:06,960
- Maybe just a trim?
- Great.

489
00:18:06,961 --> 00:18:09,170
I'm thinking a pixie cut.

490
00:18:09,171 --> 00:18:10,964
- What?
- I'm kidding.

491
00:18:10,965 --> 00:18:12,757
I cut my husband Benji's hair
all the time.

492
00:18:12,758 --> 00:18:14,259
Trust me, you're gonna look
fabulous.

493
00:18:14,260 --> 00:18:15,845
When's the last time
you had a haircut?

494
00:18:17,471 --> 00:18:20,765
Maybe my daughter's wedding
a few years ago.

495
00:18:20,766 --> 00:18:22,100
Where?

496
00:18:22,101 --> 00:18:23,310
St. Sebastian,

497
00:18:23,311 --> 00:18:25,312
Our Lady of Mount Carmel
Parish.

498
00:18:25,313 --> 00:18:27,939
Does your daughter know
where you are?

499
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:31,109
Of course.
We all live in Pittsburgh.

500
00:18:31,110 --> 00:18:33,321
In fact,
they live in my old house.

501
00:18:35,948 --> 00:18:38,283
Your daughter lives
in your house?

502
00:18:38,284 --> 00:18:40,160
Yep.

503
00:18:40,161 --> 00:18:42,704
Where do you live?

504
00:18:42,705 --> 00:18:44,874
Wherever I want.

505
00:18:46,667 --> 00:18:48,793
You're gonna pass it
5 to 6 centimeters

506
00:18:48,794 --> 00:18:51,297
from the inner table
of the skull, OK?

507
00:18:53,257 --> 00:18:55,425
Centered...

508
00:18:55,426 --> 00:18:57,260
perpendicular...

509
00:18:57,261 --> 00:18:59,055
aiming for the medial canthus.

510
00:19:00,222 --> 00:19:01,890
All yours.

511
00:19:01,891 --> 00:19:03,224
A-and just keep going?

512
00:19:03,225 --> 00:19:04,684
You'll feel a pop
when you pass

513
00:19:04,685 --> 00:19:07,270
the ependymal lining.

514
00:19:07,271 --> 00:19:09,064
Art line is calibrated.
Good to go.

515
00:19:09,065 --> 00:19:12,984
Titrate the nicardipine
to a MAP of 85, please.

516
00:19:12,985 --> 00:19:14,402
And if we can get
the intracranial pressure

517
00:19:14,403 --> 00:19:16,155
down to 20?

518
00:19:17,615 --> 00:19:19,074
Dr. Mohan?

519
00:19:19,075 --> 00:19:20,533
I'm sorry.

520
00:19:20,534 --> 00:19:22,827
MAP of 85, ICP of 20?

521
00:19:22,828 --> 00:19:25,830
Um, cerebral perfusion
pressure 65.

522
00:19:25,831 --> 00:19:28,583
Which gives him
the best shot at survival.

523
00:19:28,584 --> 00:19:30,085
A third of patients
like this die.

524
00:19:30,086 --> 00:19:32,671
Half have long-term disability.

525
00:19:32,672 --> 00:19:34,631
We'll know in two weeks
if there's a possibility

526
00:19:34,632 --> 00:19:36,966
for a good prognosis.

527
00:19:36,967 --> 00:19:38,176
Felt a pop.

528
00:19:38,177 --> 00:19:39,762
Remove the stylet.

529
00:19:42,306 --> 00:19:45,059
OK, let it drain a bit.

530
00:19:47,019 --> 00:19:49,230
And now pinch it shut.

531
00:19:50,731 --> 00:19:51,731
Perfect.

532
00:19:51,732 --> 00:19:53,608
BP is down, 190 over 88.

533
00:19:53,609 --> 00:19:54,944
Heart rate's 67.

534
00:19:59,073 --> 00:20:01,032
How are you guys doing?

535
00:20:01,033 --> 00:20:02,951
Yeah, making some progress.

536
00:20:02,952 --> 00:20:04,285
You seen Abbot?

537
00:20:04,286 --> 00:20:06,079
Not since rounds.

538
00:20:06,080 --> 00:20:08,790
He asked me to see a patient
with the night intern.

539
00:20:08,791 --> 00:20:10,417
And you said yes?

540
00:20:10,418 --> 00:20:13,294
48-year-old woman,
new onset jaundice,

541
00:20:13,295 --> 00:20:16,381
elevated liver enzymes,
no history of alcohol use.

542
00:20:16,382 --> 00:20:17,716
Take your pick--

543
00:20:17,717 --> 00:20:20,427
hepatitis A, B, C, D, or E.

544
00:20:20,428 --> 00:20:23,304
- No risk factors, no fever.
- Tylenol?

545
00:20:23,305 --> 00:20:25,181
Never,
and no prescription meds.

546
00:20:25,182 --> 00:20:27,393
Does she eat
polar bear liver?

547
00:20:28,602 --> 00:20:30,813
It can cause
vitamin A toxicity.

548
00:20:31,772 --> 00:20:32,856
- No.
- Yeah.

549
00:20:32,857 --> 00:20:34,107
She, uh, doesn't eat meat,

550
00:20:34,108 --> 00:20:35,734
kind of a health nut.

551
00:20:35,735 --> 00:20:37,152
Well, maybe
she's gulping down

552
00:20:37,153 --> 00:20:38,778
cod liver oil
to prevent measles.

553
00:20:38,779 --> 00:20:40,989
No. Vegan, no fish.

554
00:20:40,990 --> 00:20:43,033
Would you, uh, mind
laying eyes on her?

555
00:20:43,826 --> 00:20:44,826
Seriously?

556
00:20:44,827 --> 00:20:46,995
You have a way of
figuring out the weird stuff.

557
00:20:46,996 --> 00:20:48,456
Take the compliment.

558
00:20:49,874 --> 00:20:51,291
OK, fine.

559
00:20:51,292 --> 00:20:53,585
Five minutes at the bedside--
that's it.

560
00:20:53,586 --> 00:20:55,545
I'm already gonna be here
for hours as it is.

561
00:20:55,546 --> 00:20:57,797
Thank you.

562
00:20:57,798 --> 00:20:59,341
What am I doing--

563
00:21:02,553 --> 00:21:04,929
- Definitely improving.
- Tidal volume's up.

564
00:21:04,930 --> 00:21:07,432
Wheezes now expiratory only.

565
00:21:07,433 --> 00:21:09,017
Oh, making some progress.

566
00:21:09,018 --> 00:21:11,144
You feeling better, baby?

567
00:21:11,145 --> 00:21:14,397
- You scared the shit out of me.
- Language!

568
00:21:14,398 --> 00:21:16,775
Does he have
a primary-care doctor?

569
00:21:16,776 --> 00:21:18,151
Not anymore.

570
00:21:18,152 --> 00:21:20,737
How do you get
his prescriptions renewed?

571
00:21:20,738 --> 00:21:22,947
Neighborhood clinic.
We pay cash.

572
00:21:22,948 --> 00:21:24,741
- Albuterol's cheap.
- Symbicort?

573
00:21:24,742 --> 00:21:27,702
Without Medicaid,
400 bucks a month.

574
00:21:27,703 --> 00:21:29,121
Just for a little inhaler?

575
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:32,792
Trocar is on the tube.

576
00:21:33,876 --> 00:21:37,170
I tunnel underneath the scalp
about 5 centimeters

577
00:21:37,171 --> 00:21:38,671
and poke through.

578
00:21:38,672 --> 00:21:40,341
- To prevent infection?
- Mm-hmm, exactly.

579
00:21:41,926 --> 00:21:44,470
Now you hold the knuckle steady
while I pull it through.

580
00:21:47,848 --> 00:21:49,975
And you can staple
the wound shut.

581
00:21:51,477 --> 00:21:53,603
That looks like something
from Home Depot.

582
00:21:53,604 --> 00:21:55,438
Yeah, big
Fourth of July sale.

583
00:21:55,439 --> 00:21:56,773
The brain pressure
is measured by

584
00:21:56,774 --> 00:21:58,650
the height of the fluid column.

585
00:21:58,651 --> 00:22:01,194
We need to calibrate it to zero
at the level of the tragus.

586
00:22:01,195 --> 00:22:03,238
Stopcock's on,
ready to attach.

587
00:22:03,239 --> 00:22:04,614
First troponin's normal,

588
00:22:04,615 --> 00:22:07,075
but you need a second
to rule out MI.

589
00:22:07,076 --> 00:22:08,869
Hey, can you step out
for a second?

590
00:22:15,042 --> 00:22:16,501
I really did do
everything I could

591
00:22:16,502 --> 00:22:18,086
to try to make Orlando stay.

592
00:22:18,087 --> 00:22:19,087
Yeah, I don't doubt it.

593
00:22:19,088 --> 00:22:20,088
I wanted to ask you about

594
00:22:20,089 --> 00:22:22,298
Dr. Al-Hashimi at the VA.

595
00:22:22,299 --> 00:22:25,009
Did you ever notice anything
unusual about her behavior?

596
00:22:25,010 --> 00:22:27,011
Um, like what?

597
00:22:27,012 --> 00:22:29,639
Lapses in focus, attention?

598
00:22:29,640 --> 00:22:32,142
No, she was always
on top of her game.

599
00:22:35,145 --> 00:22:38,857
But this morning when she was
checking labs on Baby Jane Doe,

600
00:22:38,858 --> 00:22:41,193
it was like she zoned out
for a few seconds.

601
00:22:42,695 --> 00:22:44,446
Maybe she was just tired.

602
00:22:51,495 --> 00:22:53,830
No congestion, nodules,

603
00:22:53,831 --> 00:22:55,290
or cirrhosis.

604
00:22:55,291 --> 00:22:56,958
Good-looking liver.

605
00:22:56,959 --> 00:22:58,835
I should not be sick.

606
00:22:58,836 --> 00:23:01,462
I work so hard
to stay healthy--

607
00:23:01,463 --> 00:23:04,382
diet, exercise,
eight hours of sleep.

608
00:23:04,383 --> 00:23:08,219
I can't remember the last
time I got eight hours.

609
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:10,221
Maybe you should try
sleepmaxxing.

610
00:23:10,222 --> 00:23:12,140
Oh, you definitely should.

611
00:23:12,141 --> 00:23:15,059
Yeah, cold room,
white noise, eye shades.

612
00:23:15,060 --> 00:23:18,897
Kiwis before bedtime,
lettuce water, mouth taping.

613
00:23:18,898 --> 00:23:20,565
Who do you follow for health?

614
00:23:20,566 --> 00:23:22,901
A few naturopaths
and some functional healers.

615
00:23:22,902 --> 00:23:24,861
Do you--do you buy
vitamins from them?

616
00:23:24,862 --> 00:23:26,696
Oh, no, no,
I don't take vitamins.

617
00:23:26,697 --> 00:23:29,490
Food is the best medicine--
kale, blueberries,

618
00:23:29,491 --> 00:23:32,076
- kidney beans, turmeric.
- Turmeric?

619
00:23:32,077 --> 00:23:33,786
Uh, how long have you
been taking that?

620
00:23:33,787 --> 00:23:36,331
For a few months.
It's an anti-inflammatory.

621
00:23:36,332 --> 00:23:38,875
It detoxes the body,
and it can prevent Alzheimer's.

622
00:23:38,876 --> 00:23:40,335
How much do you take?

623
00:23:40,336 --> 00:23:42,337
500 milligram capsules,

624
00:23:42,338 --> 00:23:43,547
but I take five a day.

625
00:23:45,299 --> 00:23:46,883
What?

626
00:23:46,884 --> 00:23:48,718
With doses that large
of turmeric,

627
00:23:48,719 --> 00:23:51,346
there have been cases
of liver failure.

628
00:23:51,347 --> 00:23:53,056
From eating a spice?

629
00:23:53,057 --> 00:23:55,725
All right, Digby,
I think you're good to go.

630
00:23:55,726 --> 00:23:57,811
Mm-hmm.
Would you like to see?

631
00:24:10,449 --> 00:24:12,909
I haven't looked like this
in a long time.

632
00:24:12,910 --> 00:24:15,329
Your family
won't recognize you.

633
00:24:17,247 --> 00:24:19,415
Then how will they find me?

634
00:24:19,416 --> 00:24:21,417
They--they won't know
what I look like.

635
00:24:21,418 --> 00:24:22,502
They won't know this is me.

636
00:24:22,503 --> 00:24:23,628
Of course they will.

637
00:24:23,629 --> 00:24:24,879
They know your voice.

638
00:24:24,880 --> 00:24:26,714
They know where you hang out.

639
00:24:26,715 --> 00:24:30,551
They even remember that
you used to look like this.

640
00:24:30,552 --> 00:24:32,554
They remember the wedding.

641
00:24:35,516 --> 00:24:37,767
Did you dance
with your daughter

642
00:24:37,768 --> 00:24:39,186
at her wedding?

643
00:24:40,604 --> 00:24:42,814
I did.

644
00:24:42,815 --> 00:24:45,818
Then she will always
remember you.

645
00:24:48,570 --> 00:24:50,114
- Yeah.
- OK.

646
00:24:51,615 --> 00:24:53,241
Hey, I was just
looking for you.

647
00:24:53,242 --> 00:24:54,575
- What's up?
- You tell me.

648
00:24:54,576 --> 00:24:56,911
- The, uh, asthma patient.
- What about him?

649
00:24:56,912 --> 00:24:58,287
Seemed like
you were hesitating

650
00:24:58,288 --> 00:24:59,956
talking about using Aerogen.

651
00:24:59,957 --> 00:25:01,666
I was wondering if you were
having second thoughts.

652
00:25:01,667 --> 00:25:03,418
No. Just thinking.

653
00:25:03,419 --> 00:25:04,711
About?

654
00:25:04,712 --> 00:25:06,713
The best treatment plan
for the patient.

655
00:25:06,714 --> 00:25:08,798
And I think he's on it.

656
00:25:08,799 --> 00:25:10,299
- Anything else?
- I don't know.

657
00:25:10,300 --> 00:25:12,885
You tell me.
Anything else I need to know?

658
00:25:12,886 --> 00:25:14,138
I don't think so.

659
00:25:15,806 --> 00:25:17,348
This is Dr. Robby in the ED.

660
00:25:17,349 --> 00:25:19,058
I'm checking on a patient,
Ekins.

661
00:25:19,059 --> 00:25:21,602
We can take Larson
and Stevens off the dry-erase.

662
00:25:21,603 --> 00:25:22,645
Consider it done.

663
00:25:22,646 --> 00:25:23,855
He's in the scanner now?

664
00:25:23,856 --> 00:25:25,314
Oh, great.

665
00:25:25,315 --> 00:25:26,399
No, I was just calling
to confirm.

666
00:25:26,400 --> 00:25:27,692
Thank you.

667
00:25:27,693 --> 00:25:29,485
Any new information
from upstairs?

668
00:25:29,486 --> 00:25:30,945
Nothing we don't
already know.

669
00:25:30,946 --> 00:25:32,613
Same old story, huh?

670
00:25:32,614 --> 00:25:34,032
You think we should
take up a collection

671
00:25:34,033 --> 00:25:35,825
for Jesse for--for bail money?

672
00:25:35,826 --> 00:25:37,410
They don't usually set bail

673
00:25:37,411 --> 00:25:39,203
until after you've appeared
in front of a judge.

674
00:25:39,204 --> 00:25:41,080
With the holiday, it's not
likely to happen till Monday.

675
00:25:41,081 --> 00:25:43,249
So he's gonna be locked up
all weekend?

676
00:25:43,250 --> 00:25:44,959
That sucks.

677
00:25:44,960 --> 00:25:46,961
It does suck.

678
00:25:46,962 --> 00:25:50,006
Dr. Langdon, Grady's worse--
much worse.

679
00:25:50,007 --> 00:25:52,800
- Need an attending?
- Uh, no, we have Shen.

680
00:25:52,801 --> 00:25:54,218
Sat's down to 83.

681
00:25:54,219 --> 00:25:56,304
- What's happening?
- Give us a minute.

682
00:25:56,305 --> 00:25:57,805
He's tiring out.

683
00:25:57,806 --> 00:25:59,849
Ketamine and rock.
It's time to intubate.

684
00:25:59,850 --> 00:26:01,059
I'll call Volk.

685
00:26:01,060 --> 00:26:02,810
Ma'am, we have to put a tube

686
00:26:02,811 --> 00:26:04,062
down your son's windpipe

687
00:26:04,063 --> 00:26:05,521
so a machine
can breathe for him.

688
00:26:05,522 --> 00:26:06,856
Oh, my God.

689
00:26:06,857 --> 00:26:08,399
Hold on, hold on.

690
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:09,609
No lung sliding on the right.

691
00:26:09,610 --> 00:26:11,110
Pneumothorax.

692
00:26:11,111 --> 00:26:13,154
No need to intubate.

693
00:26:13,155 --> 00:26:14,447
What's going on?

694
00:26:14,448 --> 00:26:16,407
He has a collapsed lung.

695
00:26:16,408 --> 00:26:18,326
There was no history
of trauma

696
00:26:18,327 --> 00:26:19,827
that would have caused
pneumothorax.

697
00:26:19,828 --> 00:26:21,871
Glove up, Dr. King.

698
00:26:21,872 --> 00:26:24,207
In asthma, you can get
"air trapping."

699
00:26:24,208 --> 00:26:25,958
When the lungs can't
fully exhale,

700
00:26:25,959 --> 00:26:27,335
eventually they overinflate,

701
00:26:27,336 --> 00:26:29,253
causing some of the tiny
air sacs to burst.

702
00:26:29,254 --> 00:26:30,422
How do you fix it?

703
00:26:36,345 --> 00:26:37,262
Like that.

704
00:26:42,976 --> 00:26:45,603
It's a good thing
Dr. Conley was here.

705
00:26:45,604 --> 00:26:46,896
- Yeah.
- We should probably try

706
00:26:46,897 --> 00:26:48,439
to find him
a Neuro-Critical ICU bed.

707
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:50,024
We don't want to board
a patient like this.

708
00:26:50,025 --> 00:26:51,692
- Mm-hmm.
- Hey, Robby.

709
00:26:51,693 --> 00:26:54,278
- Hey, how did the scan go?
- Fine.

710
00:26:54,279 --> 00:26:55,738
It is probably gonna take
a little while

711
00:26:55,739 --> 00:26:57,198
to get the results
from the radiologist.

712
00:26:57,199 --> 00:26:58,658
Well, that's not a problem.

713
00:26:58,659 --> 00:27:00,868
Nurse Vivi and I need
a little time

714
00:27:00,869 --> 00:27:03,454
to coordinate our schedules
over the next few months.

715
00:27:03,455 --> 00:27:04,455
- Really?
- Yeah.

716
00:27:04,456 --> 00:27:05,456
I've always wanted to learn

717
00:27:05,457 --> 00:27:06,499
how to ride a motorcycle,

718
00:27:06,500 --> 00:27:08,000
and Duke offered to teach me.

719
00:27:08,001 --> 00:27:10,294
Well, nobody knows
motorcycles like Duke.

720
00:27:10,295 --> 00:27:12,713
He's giving me the health
care worker discount.

721
00:27:12,714 --> 00:27:14,048
He's quite the gentleman.

722
00:27:14,049 --> 00:27:15,842
Let's get him back to his room.

723
00:27:15,843 --> 00:27:18,636
How would next Saturday be
for you, Vivi?

724
00:27:18,637 --> 00:27:21,973
Uh, maybe we could have
some dinner after.

725
00:27:21,974 --> 00:27:23,599
Dr. Mohan,
Lorrie Diaz is here.

726
00:27:23,600 --> 00:27:25,351
She wants to see her husband.
She's heading back.

727
00:27:25,352 --> 00:27:26,854
OK, I'm on my way.

728
00:27:29,022 --> 00:27:31,023
- Mrs. Diaz?
- Hi.

729
00:27:31,024 --> 00:27:33,901
Did Orlando go up
to his room yet?

730
00:27:33,902 --> 00:27:35,403
No. Um--

731
00:27:35,404 --> 00:27:37,530
I brought him some dinner
from Burgatory.

732
00:27:37,531 --> 00:27:38,906
It's a chicken burger--

733
00:27:38,907 --> 00:27:40,533
no bun, just lettuce.

734
00:27:40,534 --> 00:27:43,162
Figured it would be better
than hospital food.

735
00:27:46,498 --> 00:27:50,751
He's being treated by our top
brain-injury specialists.

736
00:27:50,752 --> 00:27:52,253
Will he wake up?

737
00:27:52,254 --> 00:27:54,172
We won't know
for several weeks.

738
00:27:54,173 --> 00:27:56,757
And then he could be
back to normal?

739
00:27:56,758 --> 00:27:59,886
Best-case scenario,
it would take about a year

740
00:27:59,887 --> 00:28:02,513
before he could be
independent at home.

741
00:28:02,514 --> 00:28:04,182
And the worst case?

742
00:28:04,183 --> 00:28:07,603
Round-the-clock nursing care
for severe disability.

743
00:28:11,231 --> 00:28:13,441
You let him leave?

744
00:28:13,442 --> 00:28:17,445
He insisted on leaving
to work at his second job.

745
00:28:17,446 --> 00:28:19,655
You couldn't make him stay?

746
00:28:19,656 --> 00:28:22,658
He was competent.
He knew the risks.

747
00:28:22,659 --> 00:28:24,660
We honored his decision
to leave.

748
00:28:24,661 --> 00:28:26,454
Even if it was a stupid one?

749
00:28:26,455 --> 00:28:27,955
I tried to stop him.

750
00:28:27,956 --> 00:28:29,582
Offered to get him
all the supplies he'd need

751
00:28:29,583 --> 00:28:31,083
to take care of himself
at home.

752
00:28:31,084 --> 00:28:33,628
But he left before
I could give them to him.

753
00:28:33,629 --> 00:28:36,048
He said he couldn't afford
to lose a paycheck.

754
00:28:43,597 --> 00:28:45,766
Dr. Langdon.

755
00:28:48,018 --> 00:28:49,769
Are you OK?

756
00:28:49,770 --> 00:28:52,897
Yeah. I'm just kind of, uh...

757
00:28:52,898 --> 00:28:55,358
wondering if I'm really
ready to be back here.

758
00:28:55,359 --> 00:28:57,652
Well, of course you are.

759
00:28:57,653 --> 00:28:59,779
Ten months is a long time.

760
00:28:59,780 --> 00:29:03,032
I almost killed that kid
with an intubation.

761
00:29:03,033 --> 00:29:06,327
Didn't even occur to me
to check for pneumothorax.

762
00:29:06,328 --> 00:29:08,037
There wasn't any trauma
to indicate--

763
00:29:08,038 --> 00:29:09,164
- I should have caught it.
- OK.

764
00:29:15,921 --> 00:29:17,214
You know, I, um...

765
00:29:19,132 --> 00:29:22,051
I had a deposition today,

766
00:29:22,052 --> 00:29:25,513
and all the lawyer's questions
made me feel like

767
00:29:25,514 --> 00:29:27,808
I was a really,
really bad doctor.

768
00:29:30,185 --> 00:29:33,647
We don't always get everything
right the first time.

769
00:29:34,815 --> 00:29:37,358
You would have caught
the collapsed lung.

770
00:29:37,359 --> 00:29:39,987
And it may have taken a minute,
but you would have saved him.

771
00:29:41,238 --> 00:29:43,656
I'm not sure
Robby would agree with you.

772
00:29:43,657 --> 00:29:46,367
He's been riding me all day.

773
00:29:46,368 --> 00:29:48,244
Well, Robby's leaving
for three months.

774
00:29:48,245 --> 00:29:51,080
And, you know,
with Robby gone...

775
00:29:51,081 --> 00:29:53,041
I really don't want you
to leave either.

776
00:29:56,628 --> 00:29:59,255
That which does not kill me
makes me stronger.

777
00:29:59,256 --> 00:30:02,550
Wow, Friedrich Nietzsche.

778
00:30:02,551 --> 00:30:05,761
Yeah, Nietzsche, yeah...

779
00:30:05,762 --> 00:30:08,056
not Kelly Clarkson.

780
00:30:10,058 --> 00:30:12,059
Hey, that's a thick one.

781
00:30:12,060 --> 00:30:14,896
Yeah, Austin Green.
Ogilvie's triple-A.

782
00:30:17,941 --> 00:30:20,568
Uh, G-R-E-E-N?

783
00:30:20,569 --> 00:30:21,986
Yeah. Why?
What are you doing?

784
00:30:21,987 --> 00:30:23,446
Checking to see
when we'll get Ogilvie

785
00:30:23,447 --> 00:30:25,364
back from the OR.

786
00:30:25,365 --> 00:30:27,408
- Oh, shit.
- What?

787
00:30:27,409 --> 00:30:29,160
The guy didn't make it.

788
00:30:29,161 --> 00:30:31,454
He died on the table
about 40 minutes ago.

789
00:30:31,455 --> 00:30:33,622
Then where's Ogilvie?

790
00:30:33,623 --> 00:30:35,583
Oh, man.

791
00:30:35,584 --> 00:30:38,210
His patient had a CT
a year and a half ago

792
00:30:38,211 --> 00:30:40,504
that showed
a 4-centimeter triple-A.

793
00:30:40,505 --> 00:30:42,173
That's too small for surgery.

794
00:30:42,174 --> 00:30:43,507
He was supposed
to come back

795
00:30:43,508 --> 00:30:45,259
every six months
for a repeat ultrasound,

796
00:30:45,260 --> 00:30:46,969
but looks like he didn't.

797
00:30:46,970 --> 00:30:49,638
We would've seen that
if the computers were working.

798
00:30:49,639 --> 00:30:51,307
Why wouldn't he tell Ogilvie?

799
00:30:51,308 --> 00:30:53,184
I don't know.
Maybe he forgot all about it.

800
00:30:53,185 --> 00:30:55,145
Or Ogilvie didn't ask
the right questions.

801
00:30:56,271 --> 00:30:58,314
Dennis, hey, got a minute?

802
00:30:58,315 --> 00:31:00,858
Uh, sure. What do you need?

803
00:31:00,859 --> 00:31:02,526
Teenager with jewelry magnets

804
00:31:02,527 --> 00:31:04,528
stuck to both sides
of her nasal septum.

805
00:31:04,529 --> 00:31:06,530
I tried to move them
with a plastic curette.

806
00:31:06,531 --> 00:31:08,366
Too much pain,
and then there was bleeding.

807
00:31:08,367 --> 00:31:10,659
Those need to come off before
they cause permanent damage.

808
00:31:10,660 --> 00:31:12,244
Yeah, you think, uh,
you could find, like,

809
00:31:12,245 --> 00:31:14,163
a senior or an attending?

810
00:31:14,164 --> 00:31:16,040
We're really trying
to get off the clock here.

811
00:31:16,041 --> 00:31:17,125
They're all busy.

812
00:31:19,878 --> 00:31:21,504
I already took one
for the team.

813
00:31:21,505 --> 00:31:23,464
Yeah, fine.

814
00:31:23,465 --> 00:31:27,009
Uh, labs on your yellow lady.

815
00:31:27,010 --> 00:31:29,470
INR is elevated, 2.2.

816
00:31:29,471 --> 00:31:31,430
Liver's in trouble
but not dead yet.

817
00:31:31,431 --> 00:31:33,015
Tell her to skip
the turmeric.

818
00:31:33,016 --> 00:31:35,184
Admit for monitoring,
and follow the LFTs.

819
00:31:35,185 --> 00:31:36,394
- Got it.
- Mm-hmm.

820
00:31:36,395 --> 00:31:37,813
- Central 10?
- Yeah.

821
00:31:42,192 --> 00:31:44,360
"Sleepmaxxing"? Really?

822
00:31:44,361 --> 00:31:45,945
I track the online trends.

823
00:31:45,946 --> 00:31:48,322
Is that your secret
for the tough ones?

824
00:31:48,323 --> 00:31:50,032
I just think,

825
00:31:50,033 --> 00:31:52,410
what's the stupidest thing
this person could have done?

826
00:31:52,411 --> 00:31:53,578
Then assume they did it.

827
00:31:55,038 --> 00:31:57,248
Well, I mean,
she was trying to be healthy.

828
00:31:57,249 --> 00:31:59,583
Yeah, by taking advice
from fools.

829
00:31:59,584 --> 00:32:01,794
Turmeric is recommended
by a lot of doctors.

830
00:32:01,795 --> 00:32:03,796
Yeah, then ask your doctor
for the dose

831
00:32:03,797 --> 00:32:06,382
or check someplace reputable,
like the CDC.

832
00:32:06,383 --> 00:32:09,677
Oh, right, I forgot, it's now
a medical toxic waste site.

833
00:32:09,678 --> 00:32:12,721
I mean,
she's in pretty bad shape.

834
00:32:12,722 --> 00:32:15,015
If things get worse, she could
need a liver transplant.

835
00:32:15,016 --> 00:32:17,060
Yeah, 'cause she's a big
fucking idiot.

836
00:32:18,645 --> 00:32:20,479
Wow.

837
00:32:20,480 --> 00:32:22,731
No, I actually
appreciate her.

838
00:32:22,732 --> 00:32:25,402
Our job security depends on
all these big fucking idiots.

839
00:32:27,863 --> 00:32:29,072
OK.

840
00:32:31,408 --> 00:32:34,869
Uh, good night,
Perlah, Monica.

841
00:32:34,870 --> 00:32:37,621
- Good night, Dr. Robby.
- Good night.

842
00:32:37,622 --> 00:32:39,206
Bye, Emma.

843
00:32:39,207 --> 00:32:40,666
You could stay to pitch in.

844
00:32:40,667 --> 00:32:42,626
Mm, Dana told me
to go and get some rest

845
00:32:42,627 --> 00:32:44,044
before tomorrow's shift.

846
00:32:44,045 --> 00:32:45,713
Yeah, you had quite a day.

847
00:32:45,714 --> 00:32:47,007
Wasn't so bad.

848
00:32:49,050 --> 00:32:50,885
Why can't I find
Duke's results?

849
00:32:50,886 --> 00:32:53,637
Oh, new patient, no EHR yet.

850
00:32:53,638 --> 00:32:56,432
I can run over to Radiology,
get a printout.

851
00:32:56,433 --> 00:32:57,809
Thank you, Monica.

852
00:33:00,353 --> 00:33:02,354
Ready to pick up a few more.

853
00:33:02,355 --> 00:33:03,772
Orlando's all tucked in
for now.

854
00:33:03,773 --> 00:33:05,399
- How's he doing?
- Numbers are good.

855
00:33:05,400 --> 00:33:07,234
CPP 22.

856
00:33:07,235 --> 00:33:09,862
OK, so he's got a shot
at a decent outcome at least.

857
00:33:09,863 --> 00:33:11,489
You think he has a chance?

858
00:33:11,490 --> 00:33:13,699
Oh, I don't know
that survival was

859
00:33:13,700 --> 00:33:15,701
the outcome he was hoping for.

860
00:33:15,702 --> 00:33:17,328
What?

861
00:33:17,329 --> 00:33:19,538
He told Samira he's got
$100,000 in medical debt,

862
00:33:19,539 --> 00:33:21,958
- that his life is probably--
- Mrs. Diaz!

863
00:33:24,294 --> 00:33:26,795
- How can we help you?
- The bathroom?

864
00:33:26,796 --> 00:33:29,424
Uh, yeah.
Perlah can show you the way.

865
00:33:31,218 --> 00:33:33,636
Not a great idea to have
a private conversation

866
00:33:33,637 --> 00:33:34,887
about a patient
in a public area.

867
00:33:34,888 --> 00:33:36,889
I know. I know.

868
00:33:36,890 --> 00:33:38,265
You were
about to start yapping--

869
00:33:38,266 --> 00:33:39,768
But I didn't!

870
00:33:42,312 --> 00:33:45,272
OK.

871
00:33:45,273 --> 00:33:47,608
And how long have they
been in there?

872
00:33:47,609 --> 00:33:49,068
At least two hours.

873
00:33:49,069 --> 00:33:51,487
- How did it happen?
- With my earring.

874
00:33:51,488 --> 00:33:54,406
It was supposed to be, uh,
red, white, and blue

875
00:33:54,407 --> 00:33:56,200
to look cool at the fireworks.

876
00:33:56,201 --> 00:33:57,910
I told her for the nose,
one side only,

877
00:33:57,911 --> 00:33:59,161
but she never listens.

878
00:33:59,162 --> 00:34:00,412
This can be pretty serious.

879
00:34:00,413 --> 00:34:01,705
If we don't get them out
quickly,

880
00:34:01,706 --> 00:34:03,123
it can cut off the blood supply

881
00:34:03,124 --> 00:34:05,042
and cause the septum
to collapse.

882
00:34:05,043 --> 00:34:08,547
Like, my nose
could be deformed?

883
00:34:10,840 --> 00:34:13,425
- Oh, my God, get them off.
- Yeah, that's the plan.

884
00:34:13,426 --> 00:34:15,135
Yeah, she tried already.
It hurt like crazy.

885
00:34:15,136 --> 00:34:16,303
Because they're
stuck together

886
00:34:16,304 --> 00:34:18,430
by a very strong
magnetic force.

887
00:34:18,431 --> 00:34:20,349
- Yeah.
- No, no, no.

888
00:34:20,350 --> 00:34:22,101
Oh, uh, I'm not gonna
use the tips.

889
00:34:22,102 --> 00:34:25,145
I'm gonna flip it around
and use the handle.

890
00:34:25,146 --> 00:34:26,772
It's still gonna hurt.

891
00:34:26,773 --> 00:34:27,982
Probably not.

892
00:34:27,983 --> 00:34:29,317
Just, uh, hold still.

893
00:34:31,861 --> 00:34:33,280
OK.

894
00:34:37,534 --> 00:34:38,826
Voilà.

895
00:34:38,827 --> 00:34:41,537
- Really?
- That was amazing.

896
00:34:41,538 --> 00:34:43,372
I think another half hour,

897
00:34:43,373 --> 00:34:45,082
we can send this dry-erase
board back to storage.

898
00:34:45,083 --> 00:34:46,292
With pleasure.

899
00:34:46,293 --> 00:34:47,668
- Dr. Robinavitch?
- Yep.

900
00:34:47,669 --> 00:34:49,087
Results on your friend.

901
00:34:53,758 --> 00:34:55,885
- Fuck.
- Duke?

902
00:34:59,889 --> 00:35:01,599
Are you gonna tell him?

903
00:35:01,600 --> 00:35:03,225
I want to talk
to a surgeon first.

904
00:35:03,226 --> 00:35:05,269
Uh, Dr. Robby, I have
an update on the patient.

905
00:35:05,270 --> 00:35:06,687
Now is not a great time.

906
00:35:06,688 --> 00:35:08,105
Oh, I thought
you were going home.

907
00:35:08,106 --> 00:35:09,315
Uh, I was.

908
00:35:09,316 --> 00:35:11,066
Dr. Ogilvie is just sitting

909
00:35:11,067 --> 00:35:12,818
out in the ambulance bay
covered in blood.

910
00:35:12,819 --> 00:35:14,445
Sorry, what--
what's he doing out there?

911
00:35:14,446 --> 00:35:16,405
Kind of, uh,
staring off into space.

912
00:35:16,406 --> 00:35:17,698
I tried to talk to him,
but it was like

913
00:35:17,699 --> 00:35:19,158
- he couldn't hear me.
- Monica,

914
00:35:19,159 --> 00:35:20,743
can you stat page
CardioThoracic?

915
00:35:20,744 --> 00:35:22,871
- I'll go check on Ogilvie.
- Please.

916
00:35:25,206 --> 00:35:26,416
Oh.

917
00:35:37,844 --> 00:35:39,971
Hey, Ogilvie.

918
00:35:42,599 --> 00:35:44,600
Ogilvie...

919
00:35:44,601 --> 00:35:46,436
y-you OK, man?

920
00:35:51,524 --> 00:35:53,651
99 on 2 liters.

921
00:35:53,652 --> 00:35:55,986
Scattered end
expiratory wheezes.

922
00:35:55,987 --> 00:35:58,197
He is so much better.

923
00:35:58,198 --> 00:36:00,240
The steroids
should kick in soon.

924
00:36:00,241 --> 00:36:02,618
So he'll keep improving.

925
00:36:02,619 --> 00:36:04,953
Um, when can I go home?

926
00:36:04,954 --> 00:36:06,622
In a day or two.

927
00:36:06,623 --> 00:36:09,917
And we will, uh, discharge you
with a Symbicort inhaler.

928
00:36:09,918 --> 00:36:12,086
That should last about a month.

929
00:36:12,087 --> 00:36:14,630
Hopefully we'll be
back on Medicaid by then.

930
00:36:14,631 --> 00:36:16,674
How'd you lose it?

931
00:36:16,675 --> 00:36:20,177
They sent a redetermination
letter to our old apartment.

932
00:36:20,178 --> 00:36:22,721
It didn't get forwarded.

933
00:36:22,722 --> 00:36:24,765
When I went to pick up
his prescription,

934
00:36:24,766 --> 00:36:28,602
pharmacist told me
we were no longer covered.

935
00:36:28,603 --> 00:36:30,854
And you haven't been able
to get it back since?

936
00:36:30,855 --> 00:36:33,190
I've been trying for months.

937
00:36:33,191 --> 00:36:35,651
To get re-enrolled,
you need tax returns,

938
00:36:35,652 --> 00:36:37,069
pay stubs.

939
00:36:37,070 --> 00:36:39,988
I cut hair.
My income fluctuates.

940
00:36:39,989 --> 00:36:42,449
A lot of my regulars
are struggling,

941
00:36:42,450 --> 00:36:45,577
so it's been tough.

942
00:36:45,578 --> 00:36:47,496
Well, if you run out
of Symbicort

943
00:36:47,497 --> 00:36:49,873
before your Medicaid kicks in,
you can come back,

944
00:36:49,874 --> 00:36:52,793
and we'll, uh, set you up
with another one.

945
00:36:52,794 --> 00:36:54,795
Oh, is there
a patient in here?

946
00:36:54,796 --> 00:36:57,881
'Cause everyone in this room
looks extremely healthy to me.

947
00:36:57,882 --> 00:37:00,342
Dr. Shen and I will be
with Grady all night long.

948
00:37:00,343 --> 00:37:02,302
Yeah. Day shift, we got this.

949
00:37:02,303 --> 00:37:04,263
We're leaving you
in good hands.

950
00:37:04,264 --> 00:37:06,098
Um...

951
00:37:06,099 --> 00:37:08,517
I was really scared.

952
00:37:08,518 --> 00:37:09,644
Thank you.

953
00:37:11,354 --> 00:37:13,356
You're very welcome.

954
00:37:17,277 --> 00:37:19,863
Due to his injury,
things have changed.

955
00:37:21,322 --> 00:37:23,615
I was looking for Dr. Abbot.

956
00:37:23,616 --> 00:37:26,452
I haven't seen him
for a while.

957
00:37:26,453 --> 00:37:27,704
Excuse me.

958
00:37:30,749 --> 00:37:32,750
So now,
with a long-term disability,

959
00:37:32,751 --> 00:37:35,461
things may be easier.

960
00:37:35,462 --> 00:37:36,628
"Easier"?

961
00:37:36,629 --> 00:37:38,130
His condition
will qualify him

962
00:37:38,131 --> 00:37:39,631
for Medicare and Medicaid.

963
00:37:39,632 --> 00:37:42,134
So, moving forward,
costs should be covered,

964
00:37:42,135 --> 00:37:43,927
including home health care.

965
00:37:43,928 --> 00:37:45,262
OK.

966
00:37:45,263 --> 00:37:46,722
Perhaps this isn't
the best time--

967
00:37:46,723 --> 00:37:48,098
I just wanted to reassure you

968
00:37:48,099 --> 00:37:49,893
about future costs.

969
00:37:58,151 --> 00:37:59,568
Robby.

970
00:37:59,569 --> 00:38:01,737
Noelle.

971
00:38:01,738 --> 00:38:03,363
You're still here.

972
00:38:03,364 --> 00:38:05,699
It's not the best day
to try to get out on time.

973
00:38:05,700 --> 00:38:07,367
Mm.

974
00:38:07,368 --> 00:38:08,827
So I guess this is it
for a while.

975
00:38:08,828 --> 00:38:10,329
Unless you want
to come with me.

976
00:38:10,330 --> 00:38:12,706
No, but thank you,

977
00:38:12,707 --> 00:38:14,750
even if it isn't
a legitimate offer.

978
00:38:14,751 --> 00:38:16,251
- What do you mean?
- Oh, please.

979
00:38:16,252 --> 00:38:18,128
I know well enough
not to get in between

980
00:38:18,129 --> 00:38:20,173
a man and his vision quest.

981
00:38:21,591 --> 00:38:22,925
"Vision quest."

982
00:38:22,926 --> 00:38:26,012
That is my nice way
of putting it.

983
00:38:27,263 --> 00:38:28,639
I probably don't want to hear

984
00:38:28,640 --> 00:38:30,516
your not-so-nice way
of putting it.

985
00:38:30,517 --> 00:38:31,851
No, probably not.

986
00:38:33,603 --> 00:38:37,231
I-I hope that
this is not, um...

987
00:38:37,232 --> 00:38:38,607
about you running away from me.

988
00:38:38,608 --> 00:38:39,858
I'm a big girl.

989
00:38:39,859 --> 00:38:41,527
You can tell me
just to get lost.

990
00:38:41,528 --> 00:38:43,362
This has nothing
to do with you.

991
00:38:43,363 --> 00:38:44,655
Oh, right.

992
00:38:44,656 --> 00:38:47,367
It's the old, uh,
"it's not you, it's me"?

993
00:38:48,868 --> 00:38:51,037
In this case,
it's actually true.

994
00:38:57,252 --> 00:38:58,878
Excuse me.

995
00:39:04,968 --> 00:39:06,343
I'll see you next week?

996
00:39:06,344 --> 00:39:07,678
It's a three-month
sabbatical.

997
00:39:07,679 --> 00:39:09,639
Like I said,
I will see you next week.

998
00:39:16,312 --> 00:39:19,606
My first day here
as a med student...

999
00:39:19,607 --> 00:39:21,234
there was a patient.

1000
00:39:23,069 --> 00:39:24,820
He was a real nice guy,

1001
00:39:24,821 --> 00:39:27,656
came in with belly pain.

1002
00:39:27,657 --> 00:39:31,285
I saw a gall stone
on the ultrasound,

1003
00:39:31,286 --> 00:39:33,453
normal EKG, troponin.

1004
00:39:33,454 --> 00:39:36,832
The pain resolved,
and he was in the hall

1005
00:39:36,833 --> 00:39:38,710
when he had a cardiac arrest.

1006
00:39:41,504 --> 00:39:42,839
I couldn't save him.

1007
00:39:44,465 --> 00:39:45,884
People die.

1008
00:39:47,343 --> 00:39:50,888
And we do the best we can...

1009
00:39:50,889 --> 00:39:53,224
but people die.

1010
00:39:54,475 --> 00:39:56,436
You ever get used to it?

1011
00:39:58,229 --> 00:39:59,314
No.

1012
00:40:00,982 --> 00:40:03,817
No, you...

1013
00:40:03,818 --> 00:40:05,695
you try to accept it.

1014
00:40:07,697 --> 00:40:09,449
You try to find balance.

1015
00:40:14,913 --> 00:40:17,790
I don't know if I can take
another day like today.

1016
00:40:19,334 --> 00:40:22,711
Primary care specialty
sounds way better.

1017
00:40:22,712 --> 00:40:24,504
Pedes, maybe.

1018
00:40:24,505 --> 00:40:26,049
Yeah, maybe.

1019
00:40:27,592 --> 00:40:30,678
I know I'd be bored
out of my fucking mind.

1020
00:40:32,013 --> 00:40:36,099
Seriously, I like the challenge
of undiagnosed illness,

1021
00:40:36,100 --> 00:40:41,104
of quick decisions,
of life-saving procedures.

1022
00:40:41,105 --> 00:40:43,523
And I like being here
for people

1023
00:40:43,524 --> 00:40:45,902
on the worst days
of their lives.

1024
00:40:54,077 --> 00:40:56,119
You know what I think?

1025
00:40:56,120 --> 00:40:57,829
What?

1026
00:40:57,830 --> 00:41:00,165
I think you should go home.

1027
00:41:00,166 --> 00:41:01,583
I think you should sleep on it.

1028
00:41:01,584 --> 00:41:03,085
And I think you should
at least wait

1029
00:41:03,086 --> 00:41:04,336
till the morning to decide

1030
00:41:04,337 --> 00:41:05,755
if you want to come back.

1031
00:41:08,758 --> 00:41:11,134
I don't really want to...

1032
00:41:11,135 --> 00:41:13,762
go back in there
and see anybody.

1033
00:41:13,763 --> 00:41:14,889
Yeah.

1034
00:41:16,432 --> 00:41:19,017
OK, pull off your gown.
I'll take it in.

1035
00:41:19,018 --> 00:41:21,478
Shift is over.

1036
00:41:21,479 --> 00:41:22,939
Go home.

1037
00:41:35,827 --> 00:41:37,119
- Oh!
- Oh, God.

1038
00:41:37,120 --> 00:41:38,203
- No, I'm--I'm--
- Sorry.

1039
00:41:38,204 --> 00:41:39,621
I'm good. I'm good. I'm good.

1040
00:41:39,622 --> 00:41:41,331
There's a dummy
in a wheelchair.

1041
00:41:41,332 --> 00:41:43,209
Uh, yeah, he moves around.

1042
00:41:46,295 --> 00:41:48,505
I see I've been replaced.

1043
00:41:48,506 --> 00:41:50,048
Oh, did I take your spot?

1044
00:41:50,049 --> 00:41:51,717
- Not really, no.
- Are you sure?

1045
00:41:51,718 --> 00:41:53,176
Where the hell have you been?

1046
00:41:53,177 --> 00:41:54,803
I found Ogilvie.

1047
00:41:54,804 --> 00:41:56,096
And?

1048
00:41:56,097 --> 00:41:58,432
And he's going home.

1049
00:41:58,433 --> 00:41:59,641
That's it?

1050
00:41:59,642 --> 00:42:00,976
It's a long story.

1051
00:42:00,977 --> 00:42:02,436
Well, I got nothing but time.

1052
00:42:02,437 --> 00:42:04,604
I need to respect
his privacy.

1053
00:42:04,605 --> 00:42:06,189
Where's the fun in that?

1054
00:42:06,190 --> 00:42:08,151
- Beep. Beep, beep.
- Sorry.

1055
00:42:16,743 --> 00:42:18,160
Um, the shredder jammed.

1056
00:42:18,161 --> 00:42:21,122
Yeah, uh, try
putting it in reverse.

1057
00:42:23,499 --> 00:42:24,750
Perfect.

1058
00:42:24,751 --> 00:42:26,835
Just give it
a little love tap.

1059
00:42:26,836 --> 00:42:28,337
- OK.
- Kick it.

1060
00:42:29,505 --> 00:42:31,049
Jesus Christ.

1061
00:42:33,051 --> 00:42:35,218
Guess Mr. Digby got
a room upstairs.

1062
00:42:35,219 --> 00:42:36,678
In your dreams.

1063
00:42:36,679 --> 00:42:38,680
He's not in South 21.

1064
00:42:38,681 --> 00:42:40,098
Yeah, he is.

1065
00:42:40,099 --> 00:42:42,434
There's a new guy in the bed.

1066
00:42:42,435 --> 00:42:44,436
Short hair, clean-shaved?

1067
00:42:44,437 --> 00:42:46,855
I'll take care of it.

1068
00:42:46,856 --> 00:42:48,565
Scout film showed
obvious pathology,

1069
00:42:48,566 --> 00:42:50,108
so we ordered the CT angiogram.

1070
00:42:50,109 --> 00:42:51,777
Textbook ascending
aortic aneurysm.

1071
00:42:51,778 --> 00:42:53,612
Eight centimeters.

1072
00:42:53,613 --> 00:42:55,489
50% one-year mortality.

1073
00:42:55,490 --> 00:42:56,782
So he definitely needs
surgery.

1074
00:42:56,783 --> 00:42:57,783
If he wants to live.

1075
00:42:57,784 --> 00:42:58,825
OK, well, he's a friend,

1076
00:42:58,826 --> 00:43:00,118
so I will talk to him.

1077
00:43:00,119 --> 00:43:01,286
I'll get him admitted
to your service.

1078
00:43:01,287 --> 00:43:03,413
- Not today.
- Why not?

1079
00:43:03,414 --> 00:43:05,248
He needs to see Cardiology
and Pulmonary first

1080
00:43:05,249 --> 00:43:06,500
to be cleared for the OR.

1081
00:43:06,501 --> 00:43:08,418
They can do a stress echo,
PFTs.

1082
00:43:08,419 --> 00:43:10,670
He needs to be admitted
and evaluated as an inpatient.

1083
00:43:10,671 --> 00:43:12,339
Nothing ever gets done
over a holiday weekend.

1084
00:43:12,340 --> 00:43:13,423
He can take it easy at home.

1085
00:43:13,424 --> 00:43:14,841
He's a ticking time bomb.

1086
00:43:14,842 --> 00:43:16,176
He's probably been that way
for years.

1087
00:43:16,177 --> 00:43:17,469
We can get him in
early next week

1088
00:43:17,470 --> 00:43:19,054
with a specialist
to get his testing done.

1089
00:43:19,055 --> 00:43:21,014
All goes well, he's on
the OR schedule in a week.

1090
00:43:21,015 --> 00:43:22,641
What happens if
it ruptures before then?

1091
00:43:22,642 --> 00:43:24,476
Call 911.

1092
00:43:24,477 --> 00:43:26,144
Sorry, Robby. Best we can do.

1093
00:43:26,145 --> 00:43:28,064
Text me his number.
I'll have my office coordinate.

1094
00:43:30,274 --> 00:43:31,900
- Fuck!
- Hey!

1095
00:43:31,901 --> 00:43:33,569
Take a walk. Come on!

1096
00:43:37,907 --> 00:43:38,907
Two for discharge.

1097
00:43:38,908 --> 00:43:40,408
Yeah, please don't
ring the bell.

1098
00:43:40,409 --> 00:43:42,035
The computers are
back up and running.

1099
00:43:42,036 --> 00:43:43,578
Not for these two.

1100
00:43:43,579 --> 00:43:44,996
They don't have electronic
health records yet.

1101
00:43:44,997 --> 00:43:46,373
Wait, hold up.

1102
00:43:46,374 --> 00:43:48,625
This kid had
a wrist X-ray ordered.

1103
00:43:48,626 --> 00:43:49,876
Ugh, it never happened.

1104
00:43:49,877 --> 00:43:51,211
And water-skiing lady's

1105
00:43:51,212 --> 00:43:52,546
still waiting on a knee series.

1106
00:43:52,547 --> 00:43:53,797
I canceled the X-rays.

1107
00:43:53,798 --> 00:43:56,133
Diagnosed them both
with ultrasound.

1108
00:43:56,134 --> 00:43:57,384
Really?

1109
00:43:57,385 --> 00:43:59,136
Yeah.

1110
00:43:59,137 --> 00:44:01,596
The, uh, little boy had
a simple buckle fracture.

1111
00:44:01,597 --> 00:44:04,224
Distal radius.
He got a Velcro splint.

1112
00:44:04,225 --> 00:44:06,935
And Mrs. Stegman had
a small medial meniscus tear.

1113
00:44:06,936 --> 00:44:09,354
Knee immobilizer, crutches,
and a follow up with ortho.

1114
00:44:09,355 --> 00:44:11,690
Could have used you
on the day shift today.

1115
00:44:11,691 --> 00:44:14,109
They don't teach us a lot
of musculoskeletal ultrasound.

1116
00:44:14,110 --> 00:44:15,652
I know.

1117
00:44:15,653 --> 00:44:18,280
That's why I did electives
at Harvard and Highland.

1118
00:44:18,281 --> 00:44:21,116
Are you applying for
an ultrasound fellowship here?

1119
00:44:21,117 --> 00:44:23,910
I am,
but it is so competitive.

1120
00:44:23,911 --> 00:44:26,163
- That's what I hear.
- Kind of a long shot.

1121
00:44:26,164 --> 00:44:27,581
I only have one publication,

1122
00:44:27,582 --> 00:44:29,499
but it's a series
of case reports diagnosing

1123
00:44:29,500 --> 00:44:32,043
shoulder dislocations
with ultrasound only.

1124
00:44:32,044 --> 00:44:34,045
If you want to learn some MSK,
you can tag along.

1125
00:44:34,046 --> 00:44:35,547
I got three more to scan.

1126
00:44:35,548 --> 00:44:37,549
Maybe some other time.

1127
00:44:37,550 --> 00:44:39,886
Cool.

1128
00:44:42,305 --> 00:44:44,306
Hey, don't jam the shredder.

1129
00:44:44,307 --> 00:44:45,849
What is that, two charts?

1130
00:44:45,850 --> 00:44:48,352
No, it's my ultrasound
fellowship application.

1131
00:44:50,188 --> 00:44:51,813
Hey.

1132
00:44:51,814 --> 00:44:54,816
Uh, sorry about your patient.

1133
00:44:54,817 --> 00:44:57,819
Yeah, Orlando's
in pretty bad shape.

1134
00:44:57,820 --> 00:44:59,738
Oh, no,
I--I was talking about

1135
00:44:59,739 --> 00:45:03,326
the triple-A guy
you worked on with Ogilvie.

1136
00:45:05,953 --> 00:45:08,580
He didn't make it
through surgery.

1137
00:45:08,581 --> 00:45:10,123
I tried to talk to Robby
about it,

1138
00:45:10,124 --> 00:45:12,125
but I think he's busy.

1139
00:45:12,126 --> 00:45:13,753
Excuse me.

1140
00:45:16,130 --> 00:45:17,882
Oh, shit.

1141
00:45:22,136 --> 00:45:23,637
You think I'm on edge?

1142
00:45:23,638 --> 00:45:25,430
First you're shaming Samira,
then McKay--

1143
00:45:25,431 --> 00:45:26,765
They both needed
to be called out

1144
00:45:26,766 --> 00:45:28,099
- for unacceptable behavior.
- Yeah?

1145
00:45:28,100 --> 00:45:29,392
Yeah, well, you do that
in private.

1146
00:45:29,393 --> 00:45:30,810
Same place
you share your thoughts

1147
00:45:30,811 --> 00:45:32,020
about a patient's
possible suicide.

1148
00:45:32,021 --> 00:45:33,480
And slamming stuff? Please.

1149
00:45:33,481 --> 00:45:34,689
Sign out all the shit
that's bugging you

1150
00:45:34,690 --> 00:45:35,857
and get out of here.

1151
00:45:35,858 --> 00:45:37,692
- I can't.
- Yes, you can.

1152
00:45:37,693 --> 00:45:39,027
When either of my kids
was acting like this,

1153
00:45:39,028 --> 00:45:40,487
I gave them a time-out
in their room.

1154
00:45:40,488 --> 00:45:41,655
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
you're not my mother.

1155
00:45:41,656 --> 00:45:42,864
Yeah? Well, too bad.

1156
00:45:42,865 --> 00:45:44,074
- You need one.
- No, I had one.

1157
00:45:44,075 --> 00:45:45,784
She left.
I don't need another one.

1158
00:45:45,785 --> 00:45:47,118
What I need is someone
who can actually run this place

1159
00:45:47,119 --> 00:45:49,037
- while I'm gone.
- OK, I'm sorry.

1160
00:45:49,038 --> 00:45:50,372
- I didn't know.
- Nobody knows.

1161
00:45:50,373 --> 00:45:52,666
Who needs to know?
Who gives a fuck?

1162
00:45:52,667 --> 00:45:54,000
I think you need a break.

1163
00:45:54,001 --> 00:45:55,585
That is what
the sabbatical is for.

1164
00:45:55,586 --> 00:45:57,128
Then start it now. Walk away.

1165
00:45:57,129 --> 00:45:58,380
I have too much to do.

1166
00:45:58,381 --> 00:46:00,090
Let someone else
talk to Duke.

1167
00:46:00,091 --> 00:46:01,841
No, that needs
to come from me.

1168
00:46:01,842 --> 00:46:03,176
Why?

1169
00:46:03,177 --> 00:46:04,761
Because I owe him that.

1170
00:46:04,762 --> 00:46:06,596
It needs to come from a friend,
not a stranger,

1171
00:46:06,597 --> 00:46:08,640
otherwise he's gonna bail
and drop dead while I'm gone.

1172
00:46:08,641 --> 00:46:11,518
OK, wrap that up
and then leave.

1173
00:46:11,519 --> 00:46:13,144
It's not just Duke.

1174
00:46:13,145 --> 00:46:14,896
I'm not sure that Al-Hashimi
is fit to run this place.

1175
00:46:14,897 --> 00:46:16,106
- What's that supposed to mean?
- I'm not sure.

1176
00:46:16,107 --> 00:46:17,732
I'm trying to figure that out.

1177
00:46:17,733 --> 00:46:18,984
Did you know that she wants
to have two attendings

1178
00:46:18,985 --> 00:46:20,610
- on at all times?
- No.

1179
00:46:20,611 --> 00:46:22,112
Is that something
she's worked out with Gloria?

1180
00:46:22,113 --> 00:46:23,655
- I don't know.
- I also don't know

1181
00:46:23,656 --> 00:46:24,990
if Langdon is going to relapse.

1182
00:46:24,991 --> 00:46:25,991
I don't know if
Whitaker's gonna be able

1183
00:46:25,992 --> 00:46:27,367
to take care of my shit.

1184
00:46:27,368 --> 00:46:28,952
I don't know if
Javadi's gonna give up on

1185
00:46:28,953 --> 00:46:30,829
what she's good at
or if Samira's gonna flame out

1186
00:46:30,830 --> 00:46:32,247
because of some bullshit
with her mother.

1187
00:46:32,248 --> 00:46:34,666
- Is there anything else?
- Yeah, you.

1188
00:46:34,667 --> 00:46:36,876
I don't know about you
running around

1189
00:46:36,877 --> 00:46:38,670
with a full syringe of Versed
in your pocket.

1190
00:46:38,671 --> 00:46:41,047
I'm worried about the people
that I care about.

1191
00:46:41,048 --> 00:46:43,466
We'll all manage
until you come back.

1192
00:46:43,467 --> 00:46:44,634
We always do.

1193
00:46:44,635 --> 00:46:46,387
Yeah?
What if I don't come back?

